-- title:
--   Minimal primes of the level-zero edge chart fibre
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring, let $\pi \in \mathcal{O}$ be such that the principal ideal $(\pi)$ is maximal, and let $r$ be a natural number. Write $A =$ `chartERing 𝒪 π r`, the localisation of $\mathcal{O}[X_0,X_1] =$ `MvPolynomial (Fin 2) 𝒪` modulo the principal ideal generated by `edgeRel 𝒪 π`, away from the image `edgeQuot.discr 𝒪 π r` of the element `edgeDiscr 𝒪 r`; and let $A_0 = A/(\pi^{0+1})$ be the quotient of $A$ by the ideal generated by the first power of the image of $\pi$ under the structure map $\mathcal{O} \to A$. The assertion is: if $P$ is an ideal of $A_0$ lying in `minimalPrimes A_0`, that is, a minimal element of the set of prime ideals of $A_0$ (equivalently, a minimal prime over the zero ideal), then either $P$ is the principal ideal generated by the residue class of `chartERing.ξ 𝒪 π r` in $A_0$, or $P$ is the principal ideal generated by the residue class of `chartERing.η 𝒪 π r`.
--
--   This identifies the two branches $\xi = 0$ and $\eta = 0$ of the node in the special fibre of the standard edge chart occurring in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation, at level zero, i.e. modulo the first power of the uniformiser. It feeds the statement that the morphism of spectra associated with this level-zero quotient is smooth of relative dimension one along each minimal prime.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalOmega_chartERing_eq_span_xi_or_eq_span_eta_of_mem_minimalPrimes_level_zero.lean

